SOAPBOX: This was another last-minute remote operation from NX6T in Fallbrook.
SOAPBOX: This was an interesting GiG.  While I would always like MORE EA stations
SOAPBOX: (there are never enough), there was a decent Spanish turnout.  Because I
SOAPBOX: ran frequencies most of the time, I was frequently pleasantly surprised
SOAPBOX: when EA & CR stations would call-in, freeing me from the task of looking 
SOAPBOX: for them.
SOAPBOX: 
SOAPBOX: It was nice to run a RTTY GiG this weekend, amidst running
SOAPBOX: QSO parties and the SP-DX contest in CW.  My beef with this weekend was 
SOAPBOX: with the marginal Space-WX and Solar Flux of only 69 - something we mere 
SOAPBOX: mortals can do nothing about.  At least there was very little atmospheric 
SOAPBOX: noise this weekend making RTTY copy quite easy; then again, the slow-fading
SOAPBOX: made for a LoT of exchange repeats.  
SOAPBOX: This is the REASON I send "5NN 1234" and NoT "599 1234".
SOAPBOX: 
SOAPBOX: LooK for a write-up on this GiG at: http://WQ6X.Blogspot.com
